      "id": "001",
      "headline": "Cat Learns To Open Fridge, Now Demands Tuna On Demand, Refuses To Work For It",
      "summary": "The cat has unionized and is demanding 'treats now, work never.' Negotiations are ongoing.",
      "fullBody": "Mr. Whiskers, a domestic shorthair from Spokane, has learned to open the refrigerator using his paws. He now helps himself to tuna, cheese, and occasionally leftover chicken. His owner, Mark, attempted to negotiate a 'treats for tricks' arrangement. Mr. Whiskers walked away mid-sentence. 'He's not even pretending to negotiate,' Mark said. The cat has been spotted teaching other neighborhood cats the technique. The fridge is now baby-proofed. Mr. Whiskers is studying the lock.",
      "category": "pets",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-18/001.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "2 hrs ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 68,
      "tags": ["Pets", "Cats", "Satire"],
      "isBreaking": false
    },
    {
      "id": "002",
      "headline": "Congress Debates National 'Pants Optional' Day For 6 Hours, Forgets To Vote On Important Budget",
      "summary": "The budget expired. Pants were still optional. No one knows what happened.",
      "fullBody": "Congress spent 6 hours debating whether to declare a national 'Pants Optional Day.' The budget expired during the debate. 'This is a serious issue,' said one representative, wearing pajama pants. 'Freedom of legwear is a fundamental right.' The budget was not discussed. The budget did not pass. Pants remain mandatory for now. The next session will revisit the budget — and also pants. 'Priorities,' one senator said.",
      "category": "politics",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-18/002.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "4 hrs ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 66,
      "tags": ["Politics", "Absurd", "Satire"],
      "isBreaking": true
    },
    {
      "id": "003",
      "headline": "Woman Accidentally Trains Dog To Open Mail, Now Receives Passive-Aggressive Letters From Him",
      "summary": "'Dear Human, the mail is late. Sincerely, Your Dog.' The dog has also started paying bills.",
      "fullBody": "Amanda trained her dog, Max, to retrieve the mail. Max now opens it, reads it, and offers feedback. 'He circled the electric bill and left a paw print on it,' Amanda said. 'I think he's disappointed in me.' Max has also started paying some bills online using Amanda's laptop. 'I don't know how he learned the password,' Amanda said. Max has been seen watching financial advice videos on YouTube. 'He's fiscally responsible,' Amanda said. 'And also passive-aggressive.'",
      "category": "pets",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-18/003.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "6 hrs ago",
